00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:43.780
Well, as Daryl is explaining the dangers of the bailer.
嗯，当时达里尔正在解释打包机的危险性。

814
00:33:43.780 --> 00:33:46.860
For example, Michael is making a ton of jokes.
比如，迈克尔一直在开各种玩笑。

815
00:33:47.740 --> 00:33:49.700
Andy's trying to suck up to Dwight.
安迪在试图讨好德怀特。

816
00:33:49.920 --> 00:33:53.980
And this is when people start making bets, right?
然后就在这时候，大家开始打赌了，对吧？

817
00:33:54.180 --> 00:33:54.460
Yes.
没错。

818
00:33:54.560 --> 00:33:56.700
This is the other storyline of the whole episode.
这是整集节目的另一条故事线。

819
00:33:56.700 --> 00:34:03.100
So Daryl is about to say, do you know how many people lose an arm in a bailer each year?
所以达里尔正要说，你知道每年有多少人因为打包机失去手臂吗？

820
00:34:03.360 --> 00:34:06.740
Kevin and Jim decide to bet on what they think the answer is.
凯文和吉姆决定打赌猜答案是多少。

821
00:34:07.920 --> 00:34:08.640
Yes, exactly.
是的，没错。

822
00:34:08.820 --> 00:34:10.140
It happens around four minutes.
这发生在四分钟左右。

823
00:34:10.380 --> 00:34:14.840
I want to share with you that Mindy said something that really made me laugh in the DVD commentary.
我想和你们分享一下，明迪在DVD评论音轨里说的一句话真的让我大笑不止。

824
00:34:14.840 --> 00:34:23.760
She said that in the writer's room, they were talking about this bailer, and they really saw it as a scary, big piece of machinery.
她说在编剧室里，他们讨论过这台打包机，他们真的觉得那是一个可怕的大型机械。

825
00:34:24.100 --> 00:34:26.080
Like, maybe it had blades or something.
就好像，它可能带刀片什么的。

826
00:34:26.220 --> 00:34:29.860
And when they got it, she said it just looked like a big telephone booth.
但当他们拿到它时，她说它看起来就像个大电话亭。

827
00:34:31.080 --> 00:34:31.640
Yes.
是的。

828
00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:33.760
That moved really slowly.
而且移动得非常慢。

829
00:34:35.620 --> 00:34:42.640
Well, I talked to Kent Sabornak about this bailer, and he said that it was a real working bailer.
嗯，我跟肯特·萨博纳克聊过这台打包机，他说那是一台真正能运作的打包机。

830
00:34:42.960 --> 00:34:43.380
Yeah.
是啊。

831
00:34:43.380 --> 00:34:45.880
We had an actual safety meeting.
我们还专门开过一次安全会议。

832
00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:46.660
Remember, Jenna?
还记得吗，珍娜？

833
00:34:47.280 --> 00:34:47.500
Yes.
记得。

834
00:34:47.500 --> 00:34:53.200
When we went into the warehouse to shoot, our second AD held a safety meeting that was like, guys, we have a forklift.
当我们进入仓库拍摄时，我们的第二助理导演开了一个安全会议，大概就是说，伙计们，我们有叉车。

835
00:34:53.300 --> 00:34:54.080
We have a bailer.
我们有打包机。

836
00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:55.200
Do not touch anything.
什么都别碰。

837
00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:56.300
Yeah.
没错。

838
00:34:56.440 --> 00:34:57.800
These are real machines.
这些都是真正的机器。

839
00:34:58.940 --> 00:35:07.220
He said that he called the manufacturer Olympic Wire and Equipment, and they donated a bailer because they got, like, free product placement.
他说他给制造商奥林匹克电线与设备公司打了电话，他们捐赠了一台打包机，因为他们能获得免费的产品植入。

840
00:35:08.280 --> 00:35:09.940
So that we got a free bailer.
所以我们免费得到了一台打包机。

841
00:35:10.420 --> 00:35:18.440
Well, I want to say that there is this little part at the end of the bailer conversation where it's going on and on, right?
嗯，我想说的是，在打包机对话的结尾有一小段，对话没完没了，对吧？

842
00:35:18.600 --> 00:35:18.740
Yeah.
没错。

843
00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:21.560
And Daryl is like, so do you understand?
然后达里尔说，所以你明白了吗？

844
00:35:21.700 --> 00:35:25.820
And Michael is like, yes, only on the rarest occasion.
迈克尔说，明白，只有在极少数情况下。

845
00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:30.940
And Daryl is like, on no occasions, on no occasions.
达里尔说，任何情况下都不行，任何情况下都不行。

846
00:35:31.880 --> 00:35:35.520
I had to look that up in the script, and I will tell you that was not in the script.
我特意去查了剧本，我可以告诉你，那段不在剧本里。

847
00:35:35.620 --> 00:35:36.800
I think that was improvised.
我觉得那是即兴发挥的。

848
00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:43.740
I feel like I remember that, too, being there, and we just let Steve and Craig go back and forth.
我感觉我也记得那场戏，当时我在现场，我们就让史蒂夫和克雷格在那儿一来一回地对戏。

849
00:35:44.260 --> 00:35:45.240
Just go back and forth.
就让他们一来一回地演。

850
00:35:46.480 --> 00:35:48.820
And, you know, it brought me back, Angela.
而且，你知道，这让我想起了过去，安吉拉。

851
00:35:49.020 --> 00:35:51.700
I just loved shooting this episode.
我特别喜欢拍这一集。

852
00:35:51.700 --> 00:35:58.040
And part of it was because, if you notice, we're all in these big group scenes almost all the time.
部分原因在于，如果你注意到了，我们几乎全程都在拍这种大型群戏。

853
00:35:58.720 --> 00:35:58.880
Yeah.
没错。

854
00:35:59.500 --> 00:36:01.600
This was an episode of big group scenes.
这一集全是大型群戏。

855
00:36:01.760 --> 00:36:06.700
And not just that, we also got to work with Patrice and Craig and Carly.
不仅如此，我们还有机会和帕特里斯、克雷格以及卡莉一起合作。

856
00:36:06.820 --> 00:36:08.680
We had all the warehouse folks, too.
仓库里的伙计们也都来了。

857
00:36:08.900 --> 00:36:10.540
We were all together all the time.
我们一直都在一起。

858
00:36:10.540 --> 00:36:12.400
And it really is rare.
这真的很难得。

859
00:36:12.540 --> 00:36:14.260
I mean, it happened in the basketball episode.
我是说，篮球那一集出现过这种情况。

860
00:36:14.260 --> 00:36:15.420
It happened in this one.
这一集也出现了。

861
00:36:15.800 --> 00:36:17.800
Some Christmas parties and things like that.
还有一些圣诞派对之类的场合。

862
00:36:17.880 --> 00:36:21.060
But it was rare, and we would all just have a great time.
但这确实很少见，我们在一起总是玩得很开心。

863
00:36:21.760 --> 00:36:26.980
And I liked it, too, because it was such a simple idea.
我也很喜欢这一集，因为它构思非常简单。

864
00:36:26.980 --> 00:36:28.820
It's just safety training day.
就是安全培训日。

865
00:36:28.940 --> 00:36:29.200
I know.
我知道。

866
00:36:29.340 --> 00:36:29.760
That's it.
就这么简单。

867
00:36:29.860 --> 00:36:35.700
And it goes off the rails, and we're all in, like, all of us are now can't get any work done.
结果事情完全失控了，我们所有人都没法干活了。

868
00:36:35.920 --> 00:36:36.040
Yeah.
是啊。

869
00:36:36.340 --> 00:36:42.120
Well, I have to say, before we leave this scene, I absolutely love that Michael cannot remember Madge's name.
好吧，我得说，在离开这个场景之前，我特别喜欢迈克尔记不住玛奇名字的桥段。

870
00:36:42.500 --> 00:36:43.260
He can't.
他确实记不住。

871
00:36:43.640 --> 00:36:44.080
No.
没错。

872
00:36:44.160 --> 00:36:46.440
He calls her Patch, Pudge.
他管她叫帕奇、帕奇（Pudge）。

873
00:36:46.800 --> 00:36:48.460
He cannot remember her name.
他就是记不住她的名字。

874
00:36:48.860 --> 00:36:53.440
My mom cannot remember a name that is just slightly different.
我妈也记不住那种稍微有点不一样的名字。

875
00:36:53.960 --> 00:36:54.940
Just slightly different.
就只是稍微有点不同。

876
00:36:55.520 --> 00:36:56.520
Here's an example.
举个例子。

877
00:36:56.980 --> 00:37:02.920
When I was in college, my roommate's boyfriend's name was Bart, B-A-R-T, Bart.
我上大学的时候，我室友的男朋友叫巴特（Bart），B-A-R-T，巴特。

878
00:37:03.480 --> 00:37:03.880
Okay.
好的。

879
00:37:04.060 --> 00:37:06.400
And the day I met him, my mom was with me.
我见到他的那天，我妈也在场。

880
00:37:06.500 --> 00:37:10.660
And the minute he was like, hi, I'm Bart, I thought, nope, not going to happen.
他刚一说“嗨，我是巴特”，我就心想，完了，肯定记不住了。

881
00:37:11.060 --> 00:37:12.520
Nope, it's never going to get that one.
不行，她永远也记不住这个名字。

882
00:37:12.680 --> 00:37:13.280
What did she call him?
她管他叫什么？

883
00:37:13.420 --> 00:37:16.740
For years, for years, she called him Mart.
好几年，整整好几年，她都管他叫马特（Mart）。

884
00:37:17.580 --> 00:37:18.120
How's Mart?
马特怎么样了？

885
00:37:18.560 --> 00:37:19.580
I'm like, mom, it's Bart.
我说，妈，他叫巴特。

886
00:37:19.820 --> 00:37:20.480
What did I say?
我说什么了吗？

887
00:37:20.920 --> 00:37:21.780
You said Mart.
你说的是马特。

888
00:37:22.040 --> 00:37:22.500
I did?
我说了吗？

889
00:37:22.820 --> 00:37:23.760
Yes, you did.
是的，你说了。

890
00:37:26.740 --> 00:37:29.060
Well, who would name their child Mart?
好吧，谁会给孩子起名叫马特呢？

891
00:37:29.440 --> 00:37:30.340
I don't know.
我不知道。

892
00:37:30.620 --> 00:37:31.520
I don't know.
我也不知道。

893
00:37:31.640 --> 00:37:33.500
But like, who would name their kid Patch?
但话说回来，谁会给孩子起名叫帕奇（Patch）呢？

894
00:37:33.700 --> 00:37:34.600
Or Padge?
或者是帕奇（Padge）？

895
00:37:34.760 --> 00:37:35.440
Or Pudge?
或者是帕奇（Pudge）？

896
00:37:35.620 --> 00:37:36.820
It's like...
就像是……

897
00:37:36.820 --> 00:37:37.680
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

898
00:37:37.820 --> 00:37:41.320
By the way, I apologize in advance for our listener named Mart.
顺便说一下，我先向我们名叫马特的听众道个歉。

899
00:37:41.320 --> 00:37:43.880
I would also like to apologize to anyone named Patch.
我也想向所有名叫帕奇的人道歉。

900
00:37:44.140 --> 00:37:45.040
Or Pudge.
或者叫帕奇（Pudge）的人。

901
00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:47.740
Well, now we're going to go upstairs, Angela.
好了，安吉拉，现在我们要上楼了。

902
00:37:48.360 --> 00:37:50.760
Toby is going to teach his safety meeting.
托比要开始他的安全会议了。

903
00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:56.100
For whatever reason, Michael has forced everyone from the warehouse to come to this presentation.
不知为何，迈克尔强迫仓库里的所有人都来参加这次演示。

904
00:37:56.400 --> 00:37:59.020
Paul Lieberstein knocks this out of the park.
保罗·利伯斯坦这次表现得太棒了。

905
00:37:59.180 --> 00:38:03.940
As great as Daryl was in the warehouse, Paul is as Toby in the office.
达里尔在仓库里有多棒，保罗在办公室里演托比就有多棒。

906
00:38:04.420 --> 00:38:04.660
Yes.
是的。

907
00:38:04.740 --> 00:38:07.520
His list of things, guys, to be prepared for.
伙计们，这是他准备的清单。

908
00:38:07.720 --> 00:38:08.480
Are you ready for them?
你们准备好了吗？

909
00:38:09.400 --> 00:38:10.980
Toby's office safety training.
托比的办公室安全培训。

910
00:38:11.540 --> 00:38:12.800
Carpal tunnel syndrome.
腕管综合征。

911
00:38:13.960 --> 00:38:14.920
Poor circulation.
血液循环不良。

912
00:38:16.320 --> 00:38:18.340
Computer, screen, eye strain.
电脑、屏幕、眼睛疲劳。

913
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:22.540
And you might want to keep a sweater or a cardigan in case it gets drafty.
你们可能想准备一件毛衣或开衫，以防有穿堂风。

914
00:38:23.640 --> 00:38:23.820
Yeah.
没错。

915
00:38:24.860 --> 00:38:26.160
Michael is so frustrated.
迈克尔非常沮丧。

916
00:38:26.520 --> 00:38:27.460
He can't take it.
他受不了了。

917
00:38:27.460 --> 00:38:31.480
None of these things are as exciting as getting your arm cut off in a bailer.
这些东西远没有被打包机切断手臂来得刺激。

918
00:38:31.580 --> 00:38:32.300
He can't take it.
他受不了了。

919
00:38:32.380 --> 00:38:37.280
At 5 minutes, 52 seconds, Ryan says, what about a long-sleeved tee?
在5分52秒时，瑞安问，那长袖T恤怎么样？

920
00:38:37.920 --> 00:38:38.400
Yeah.
没错。

921
00:38:38.840 --> 00:38:40.220
Here's a great story about that.
关于这一点有个很棒的故事。

922
00:38:40.620 --> 00:38:45.020
According to BJ, there was a huge joke debate about that line.
据BJ说，关于这句台词曾有过一场激烈的争论。

923
00:38:45.180 --> 00:38:46.480
What about a long-sleeved tee?
长袖T恤怎么样？

924
00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:48.220
And at 2 a.m.
当时是凌晨两点。

925
00:38:48.240 --> 00:38:49.880
in the writer's room, they were debating it.
在编剧室里，他们还在争论这个问题。

926
00:38:50.100 --> 00:38:53.260
Mike Schur said, no, this is a ridiculous line.
迈克·舒尔说，不，这台词太荒谬了。

927
00:38:53.480 --> 00:38:55.300
And Greg was all for it.
但格雷格非常支持。

928
00:38:58.320 --> 00:39:01.360
This is so funny that they spent time debating this line.
他们花时间争论这句台词真是太搞笑了。

929
00:39:01.600 --> 00:39:01.900
I know.
我知道。

930
00:39:02.100 --> 00:39:02.460
I know.
我知道。

931
00:39:02.580 --> 00:39:03.720
I love this line.
我喜欢这句台词。

932
00:39:03.980 --> 00:39:04.620
Me too.
我也是。

933
00:39:04.640 --> 00:39:06.180
And it gets called back later.
而且后来还有呼应。

934
00:39:06.180 --> 00:39:06.540
I know.
我知道。

935
00:39:06.800 --> 00:39:07.660
When we're asked to go downstairs.
当我们被要求下楼的时候。

936
00:39:08.060 --> 00:39:08.110
I know.
我知道。

937
00:39:08.240 --> 00:39:08.760
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

938
00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:20.420
Well, maybe that's why BJ delivered it so wryly, is because he knew the backstory of this debate in the writer's room over that line.
嗯，也许这就是为什么BJ说得那么讽刺，因为他知道编剧室里关于这句台词的争论背景。

939
00:39:20.420 --> 00:39:24.960
We had a fan question about another line in this little bit.
我们收到一个粉丝提问，关于这段戏里的另一句台词。

940
00:39:25.200 --> 00:39:25.360
Okay.
好的。

941
00:39:26.560 --> 00:39:35.300
Sarah Bell, Dagny Albano, and Katie Boyd all asked, when Michael's reading the safety booklet and he says office life causes a sedimentary lifestyle,
莎拉·贝尔、达格尼·阿尔巴诺和凯蒂·博伊德都问，当迈克尔读安全手册说办公室生活会导致“沉积式”生活方式时，

942
00:39:35.300 --> 00:39:38.120
was that improv or was that in the script?
那是即兴发挥还是剧本里写的？

943
00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:39.880
That was not in the script.
那不是剧本里的。

944
00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:40.700
You're kidding.
你开玩笑吧。

945
00:39:41.240 --> 00:39:48.020
There's a little bit of banter there between Michael and Toby that looks like it veered a little bit off script, like they were having a little fun with it.
迈克尔和托比之间有一点互动看起来有点脱离剧本，就像他们玩得很开心一样。

946
00:39:48.120 --> 00:39:48.960
Oh, I love that.
噢，我喜欢那个。

947
00:39:49.160 --> 00:39:50.420
So, Michael has had it.
所以，迈克尔受够了。

948
00:39:50.560 --> 00:39:51.460
He takes over.
他接管了会议。

949
00:39:51.620 --> 00:39:54.140
He's like, Toby, I'm going to do the safety training.
他说，托比，我要来做这个安全培训。

950
00:39:54.420 --> 00:39:58.500
And he wants to show the warehouse people that working in an office is just as dangerous.
他想向仓库员工证明，在办公室工作也同样危险。

951
00:39:59.500 --> 00:40:02.640
And he says, oh, there's seasonal affective disorder.
他说，哦，有季节性情绪失调这回事。

952
00:40:03.020 --> 00:40:05.060
Like dim light can lead to depression.
就像昏暗的光线会导致抑郁一样。

953
00:40:05.760 --> 00:40:07.860
And the warehouse people, they're out.
仓库那边的人都出去了。

954
00:40:08.080 --> 00:40:09.980
They're like, yeah, dim light's a bitch.
他们说，没错，昏暗的光线真要命。

955
00:40:09.980 --> 00:40:14.940
You live a little sweet nerfy life, sitting on your biscuit, never having to risk it.
你过着那种安逸的小日子，坐在那儿吃喝玩乐，从不用去冒险。

956
00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:20.260
And Michael is, he's just so bummed out.
迈克尔真的非常沮丧。

957
00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:27.260
He really wanted to prove to these guys that things get just as crazy up in the office.
他真的很想向这些人证明，办公室里的生活也一样疯狂。

958
00:40:28.460 --> 00:40:30.520
It's such a weird thing to take a stand on.
为了这种事去坚持立场真是太奇怪了。

959
00:40:30.620 --> 00:40:31.060
I know.
我知道。

960
00:40:31.440 --> 00:40:36.340
It's such a Michael Scott thing to become so invested in this.
这确实是迈克尔·斯科特会投入其中的那种事。

961
00:40:36.460 --> 00:40:38.040
He just wants to be cool, Jenna.
他只是想耍酷，珍娜。

962
00:40:38.760 --> 00:40:40.940
He's fascinated by the warehouse guys.
他被仓库那帮人迷住了。

963
00:40:41.140 --> 00:40:41.400
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

964
00:40:41.580 --> 00:40:41.940
He really is.
他确实如此。

965
00:40:42.060 --> 00:40:44.360
And this tracks from previous episodes.
这在之前的剧集里就有迹可循。

966
00:40:44.360 --> 00:40:47.240
