Like, I guess he's just gone pee, which is so on brand for Creed that he just went over to the bushes to take a whiz with his co-workers right there.
我想他大概是去撒尿了，这太符合克里德的风格了，他就在同事们旁边，跑到灌木丛里去撒尿。

1658
01:12:16.380 --> 01:12:19.800
Anyway, he says, guys, what's up with the bouncy castle?
总之，他说，伙计们，那个充气城堡是怎么回事？

1659
01:12:20.020 --> 01:12:20.800
And they're like, what?
他们说，什么？

1660
01:12:21.160 --> 01:12:22.340
They all run over.
他们全都跑了过去。

1661
01:12:22.340 --> 01:12:26.120
And this is the moment where Jim and Pam are like, oh, my God.
就在这一刻，吉姆和帕姆心想，天哪。

1662
01:12:26.300 --> 01:12:27.260
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1663
01:12:27.840 --> 01:12:29.480
He's, it's part of this bit.
他，这是那个桥段的一部分。

1664
01:12:29.640 --> 01:12:30.740
He's going to do it.
他要动手了。

1665
01:12:30.740 --> 01:12:38.460
And, well, lady, I remember shooting the scene because it is not in the script that Creed comes around the corner zipping up his pants.
嗯，女士，我记得拍摄那一幕的时候，剧本里并没有写克里德从拐角处走出来拉裤子拉链。

1666
01:12:39.120 --> 01:12:41.580
And we came up with that on the day.
那是我们当天临时想出来的。

1667
01:12:41.780 --> 01:12:45.760
We thought it would be really funny that Creed was taking a leak.
我们觉得克里德去撒尿会非常搞笑。

1668
01:12:46.300 --> 01:12:47.560
And that's how he discovered.
而他就是这样发现的。

1669
01:12:48.140 --> 01:12:49.820
And that's how he discovers it.
他就是这样发现的。

1670
01:12:49.900 --> 01:12:51.920
Because it was like, well, why is Creed around the corner?
因为当时在想，克里德为什么会在拐角那边？

1671
01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:53.860
And we're like in the moment you realize, like, how?
我们当时就在想，你意识到那一刻，怎么说呢？

1672
01:12:54.160 --> 01:12:57.700
Oh, wait, how do we justify that Creed went behind the bushes?
哦，等等，我们该怎么解释克里德去了灌木丛后面？

1673
01:12:57.840 --> 01:12:58.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1674
01:12:58.000 --> 01:13:00.820
And we thought that was so funny.
我们觉得那太搞笑了。

1675
01:13:01.060 --> 01:13:02.520
We thought that was so Creed.
我们觉得那太克里德了。

1676
01:13:02.860 --> 01:13:04.300
So I loved that.
所以我很喜欢那个设计。

1677
01:13:04.600 --> 01:13:13.060
And then I also loved that Pam tells Michael that he has to come down because she has a present for him.
我还喜欢帕姆告诉迈克尔他必须下来，因为她有礼物要给他。

1678
01:13:13.620 --> 01:13:15.700
And he never doesn't believe her.
而他从来都不会怀疑她。

1679
01:13:17.080 --> 01:13:22.960
Well, you know, Jenna, I found it interesting because when I was watching this again, all I could think of is where's Karen?
嗯，你知道吗，珍娜，我觉得很有趣，因为我重看这一集时，满脑子都在想凯伦去哪了？

1680
01:13:23.520 --> 01:13:26.560
Like Jim and Pam are sort of together in this moment.
吉姆和帕姆在这一刻好像是在一起的。

1681
01:13:26.560 --> 01:13:31.460
They're figuring out what Michael's up to and sort of brainstorming how to help him.
他们正在弄清楚迈克尔在搞什么鬼，并商量着怎么帮他。

1682
01:13:31.940 --> 01:13:33.440
And where is Karen?
那凯伦在哪？

1683
01:13:33.780 --> 01:13:34.140
Right?
对吧？

1684
01:13:34.840 --> 01:13:37.560
Well, you are not the only person who was curious about that, Angela.
嗯，安吉拉，不止你一个人对此感到好奇。

1685
01:13:37.720 --> 01:13:38.520
We got mail on that.
我们收到了关于这个问题的来信。

1686
01:13:38.640 --> 01:13:38.980
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1687
01:13:40.000 --> 01:13:47.540
Kira Bailey, Rachel Ross, Maggie June, Sarah Hamilton, and Megan Womble all asked, where's Karen?
基拉·贝利、瑞秋·罗斯、玛吉·琼、莎拉·汉密尔顿和梅根·沃布尔都问了，凯伦去哪了？

1688
01:13:48.120 --> 01:13:48.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1689
01:13:48.440 --> 01:13:59.760
Why is Jim only standing with Pam and talking with Pam and then we don't see Karen again until the end of the episode when she's on the other side of Jim standing behind him?
为什么吉姆只和帕姆站在一起，只和帕姆说话，然后直到这集结尾，我们才看到凯伦站在吉姆身后的另一边？

1690
01:14:00.380 --> 01:14:00.580
Yeah.
是啊。

1691
01:14:00.860 --> 01:14:05.980
I went to the script, Ange, and there is a whole plot for Karen that is not in this episode.
我查了剧本，安吉，凯伦确实有一整条剧情线没出现在这一集里。

1692
01:14:06.220 --> 01:14:13.420
You know how Karen earlier in the episode, she has that line where she says, wow, I do not know the people in this office like I thought I did.
你知道凯伦在这一集早些时候有句台词，她说，哇，我并不像我想象的那样了解办公室里的这些人。

1693
01:14:13.420 --> 01:14:15.440
Yeah, because she's losing all the bets.
是啊，因为她把赌注全输光了。

1694
01:14:15.620 --> 01:14:16.580
She's betting wrong.
她赌错了。

1695
01:14:16.620 --> 01:14:22.300
And she has a talking head where she's like, I am like, I'm getting wiped clean here on these bets.
她还有一个采访镜头，她说，我简直，我在这些赌局里输得精光。

1696
01:14:22.420 --> 01:14:23.280
I don't know everyone.
我不了解大家。

1697
01:14:24.100 --> 01:14:24.620
Yes.
没错。

1698
01:14:25.120 --> 01:14:31.040
So they have this whole plot for her where she's down in the parking lot and she's on a mission to get to know people better.
所以他们为她设计了整条剧情线，她在停车场里，一心想要更好地了解大家。

1699
01:14:31.380 --> 01:14:34.300
So she's starting conversations with different people.
所以她开始和不同的人搭话。

1700
01:14:34.540 --> 01:14:37.480
She's got a little side conversation with Oscar.
她和奥斯卡还有一段小插曲。

1701
01:14:37.480 --> 01:14:42.440
So I think that's why she's not standing by Jim.
所以我认为这就是她没有站在吉姆那边的原因。

1702
01:14:43.560 --> 01:14:46.600
But those scenes are not in the deleted scenes, right?
但那些场景不在删减片段里，对吧？

1703
01:14:46.960 --> 01:14:47.820
They are not.
确实不在。

1704
01:14:47.840 --> 01:14:52.360
I watched the deleted scenes and that Karen runner is not in it.
我看了删减片段，里面没有凯伦的那条线。

1705
01:14:52.660 --> 01:14:57.740
Well, one thing I did find that I thought was really fascinating and I loved this.
嗯，我确实发现了一件事，我觉得非常迷人，而且我很喜欢。

1706
01:14:57.940 --> 01:14:59.260
I'll share it with you guys.
我要和你们分享一下。

1707
01:14:59.420 --> 01:15:02.940
And it's about the Jim Pam parking lot sort of story.
是关于吉姆和帕姆在停车场的那段故事。

1708
01:15:03.640 --> 01:15:13.260
In the DVD commentary, BJ said he talked to Greg and Greg was talking to him about Jim and Pam in this scene.
在DVD评论音轨里，BJ说他跟格雷格聊过，格雷格当时在跟他讨论这一幕里的吉姆和帕姆。

1709
01:15:13.340 --> 01:15:20.640
And he said, I sort of see them as a couple that had been together for a long time and they'd had a child together.
他说，我把他们看作是一对在一起很久并且共同抚养了一个孩子的伴侣。

1710
01:15:20.860 --> 01:15:22.600
And that child is Michael.
而那个孩子就是迈克尔。

1711
01:15:23.480 --> 01:15:25.580
And, you know, they're no longer together.
而且，你知道，他们已经分开了。

1712
01:15:25.940 --> 01:15:26.800
They've moved on.
他们已经各自向前看了。

1713
01:15:27.800 --> 01:15:36.200
But like oftentimes divorced couples who have kids, when there's a crisis with their child, they work together to help their child.
但就像很多有孩子的离异夫妻一样，当孩子遇到危机时，他们会齐心协力去帮助孩子。

1714
01:15:36.380 --> 01:15:40.040
And they sort of have this shorthand with one another when it comes to their child.
在面对孩子时，他们之间有一种心照不宣的默契。

1715
01:15:40.300 --> 01:15:45.140
And Karen would not have known any of that history or Michael the way they know Michael.
而凯伦根本不知道这段历史，也不像他们那样了解迈克尔。

1716
01:15:45.140 --> 01:15:53.820
And so it made sense that Jim and Pam would be working together to try to make sure that Michael doesn't do something really stupid.
所以吉姆和帕姆联手确保迈克尔不会做出什么蠢事，这就说得通了。

1717
01:15:54.200 --> 01:15:57.960
And if you think about it in that context, it makes perfect sense.
如果你从这个角度去想，一切就完全合理了。

1718
01:15:58.140 --> 01:16:02.320
And also the fact that Pam is like, I have a present for you.
还有帕姆说“我有个礼物给你”这一点。

1719
01:16:02.600 --> 01:16:04.380
That's very parent mode, right?
那非常有家长的感觉，对吧？

1720
01:16:04.980 --> 01:16:05.360
Yeah.
没错。

1721
01:16:05.680 --> 01:16:05.900
Come inside.
进来吧。

1722
01:16:05.940 --> 01:16:07.920
I've got a treat for you.
我有个好东西给你。

1723
01:16:08.320 --> 01:16:10.020
Stop doing what you're doing.
别再做你现在做的事了。

1724
01:16:11.240 --> 01:16:23.740
I love hearing what BJ's thought process was when he was writing these scenes, because something I really appreciated about them was that Pam and Jim were not laughing about this.
我喜欢听BJ在写这些场景时的心路历程，因为我非常欣赏的一点是，帕姆和吉姆并没有拿这件事开玩笑。

1725
